10110
07:41:01.610 --> 07:41:04.900
Nice.

10111
07:41:04.900 --> 07:41:09.320
I think one thing I am sort of reflecting on,

10112
07:41:09.320 --> 07:41:12.200
as we built this our very first game,

10113
07:41:12.200 --> 07:41:15.320
is there's so many different aspects

10114
07:41:15.320 --> 07:41:17.040
of running iGame Studio.

10115
07:41:17.040 --> 07:41:19.480
Or I guess if we're even generalizing,

10116
07:41:19.480 --> 07:41:21.800
running a business, starting a startup,

10117
07:41:21.800 --> 07:41:24.440
takes really a lot of effort.

10118
07:41:24.440 --> 07:41:25.600
You have to spend a lot of time

10119
07:41:25.600 --> 07:41:28.160
building the product, doing engineering work.

10120
07:41:28.160 --> 07:41:29.960
You have to think about, you have

10121
07:41:29.960 --> 07:41:31.160
to validate your ideas.

10122
07:41:31.160 --> 07:41:33.640
You have to do GTM, go to market.

10123
07:41:33.640 --> 07:41:35.760
You have to think about monetization.

10124
07:41:35.760 --> 07:41:37.040
There's all these different things

10125
07:41:37.040 --> 07:41:41.720
that you have to consider for building a product.

10126
07:41:41.720 --> 07:41:43.560
And not just that, but also all the work

10127
07:41:43.560 --> 07:41:45.200
that goes into maintaining a product,

10128
07:41:45.200 --> 07:41:48.800
like getting feedback and whatnot.

10129
07:41:48.800 --> 07:41:55.440
So I think I'm curious what you all think about this.

10130
07:41:55.440 --> 07:41:58.040
Right now, we have a game studio.

10131
07:41:58.040 --> 07:42:01.360
But if we were to start a new business,

10132
07:42:01.360 --> 07:42:04.040
how would you think about approaching it differently

10133
07:42:04.040 --> 07:42:08.650
or whatever, based on what we learned during this experience?

10134
07:42:08.650 --> 07:42:11.490
Yeah, so I think my learnings off the top were,

10135
07:42:11.490 --> 07:42:13.330
number one, once we aligned on an idea

10136
07:42:13.330 --> 07:42:14.290
that we're all excited about,

10137
07:42:14.290 --> 07:42:15.570
and just started shipping an MVP,

10138
07:42:15.570 --> 07:42:17.130
things started moving a lot faster.

10139
07:42:17.130 --> 07:42:20.210
They were kind of like deliberating an idea.

10140
07:42:20.210 --> 07:42:22.850
And candidly, right, we had distribution

10141
07:42:22.850 --> 07:42:24.450
because we had a lot of people watching our stream.

10142
07:42:24.450 --> 07:42:26.730
So it was easy to get people to try our product.

10143
07:42:26.730 --> 07:42:29.690
I think the hardest part is really getting people to care

10144
07:42:29.690 --> 07:42:31.650
or building something that people care about.

10145
07:42:31.650 --> 07:42:33.450
For example, would anyone have played this game

10146
07:42:33.450 --> 07:42:34.610
had we not been on a live stream?

10147
07:42:34.610 --> 07:42:35.490
I do not think so.

10148
07:42:35.490 --> 07:42:36.490
I don't think so.

10149
07:42:36.490 --> 07:42:39.410
So the hardest part is getting people to care,

10150
07:42:39.410 --> 07:42:41.250
aligning on an idea that resonates with people.

10151
07:42:41.250 --> 07:42:43.210
And I really do think it is kind of like the idea,

10152
07:42:43.210 --> 07:42:45.170
like when we announced we were doing this live stream,

10153
07:42:45.170 --> 07:42:50.010
we got such a magnetic, such a compounding response.

10154
07:42:50.010 --> 07:42:51.210
It's kind of like, if you get an idea

10155
07:42:51.210 --> 07:42:53.010
that gets people really excited,

10156
07:42:53.010 --> 07:42:55.290
then you have the beginnings of something

10157
07:42:55.290 --> 07:42:58.530
that you can then create a business from, I think.

10158
07:42:58.530 --> 07:42:59.370
Yeah.

10159
07:42:59.370 --> 07:43:00.490
And I think what was interesting to me

10160
07:43:00.490 --> 07:43:02.890
is we had a bunch of talks throughout the last few days

10161
07:43:02.890 --> 07:43:05.530
where we heard from people who are using GrokBox.

10162
07:43:05.530 --> 07:43:07.890
SpaceX and our employees were using GrokBox in really fun ways.

10163
07:43:07.890 --> 07:43:09.930
And at first, I kind of thought a lot of that stuff

10164
07:43:09.930 --> 07:43:11.970
wouldn't generalize to what we did.

10165
07:43:11.970 --> 07:43:14.250
There's a lot of, well, working at a big company,

10166
07:43:14.250 --> 07:43:16.570
but it turns out a lot of the stuff was pretty relevant.

10167
07:43:16.570 --> 07:43:20.130
So the chats we had earlier today, chatting with Matt,

10168
07:43:20.130 --> 07:43:22.130
who works on our revenue operations team

10169
07:43:22.130 --> 07:43:23.930
about how you go build a growth playbook,

10170
07:43:23.930 --> 07:43:25.490
we came up with a pretty good plan

10171
07:43:25.490 --> 07:43:26.570
with some really good ideas, right?

10172
07:43:26.570 --> 07:43:28.090
Like anytime someone follows us on X,

10173
07:43:28.090 --> 07:43:29.170
we can send them a DM

10174
07:43:29.170 --> 07:43:31.810
and let them know they should try the game.

10175
07:43:31.810 --> 07:43:34.010
You know, there's a lot of like really rich ideas here,

10176
07:43:34.010 --> 07:43:35.850
then some partnership models where we could go talk

10177
07:43:35.850 --> 07:43:38.930
to companies that host games or distributors of games

10178
07:43:38.930 --> 07:43:40.450
so that we could get featured on those lists

10179
07:43:40.450 --> 07:43:41.450
or in those places.

10180
07:43:42.370 --> 07:43:44.410
I think it's kind of a standard business playbook

10181
07:43:44.410 --> 07:43:45.250
in a lot of ways, right?

10182
07:43:45.250 --> 07:43:47.290
Like you sort of can run a general business playbook.

10183
07:43:47.290 --> 07:43:49.570
You need sales, you need partnerships,

10184
07:43:49.570 --> 07:43:51.530
you need, you know, revenue operations.

10185
07:43:51.530 --> 07:43:52.890
And that probably looks and feels different

10186
07:43:52.890 --> 07:43:54.250
when you're a small zero to one company.

10187
07:43:54.250 --> 07:43:55.530
Like maybe that's all one role

10188
07:43:55.530 --> 07:43:56.850
instead of like three different roles.

10189
07:43:56.850 --> 07:43:59.410
But one thing that I really appreciated is that

10190
07:44:00.410 --> 07:44:01.610
there's a lot more work that goes into this

10191
07:44:01.610 --> 07:44:02.650
than you might expect.

10192
07:44:02.650 --> 07:44:05.090
And there's a lot of like small things to get right.

10193
07:44:05.090 --> 07:44:06.650
And, you know, I think, yeah,

10194
07:44:06.650 --> 07:44:08.650
just kind of learning those lessons

10195
07:44:08.650 --> 07:44:11.330
and being able to experience them was really cool.

10196
07:44:11.330 --> 07:44:12.170
Yeah, it's kind of interesting.

10197
07:44:12.170 --> 07:44:13.650
Like you have to go out as a human

10198
07:44:13.650 --> 07:44:16.170
and like discover all the problems organically.

10199
07:44:16.170 --> 07:44:18.050
And once you like figured out how to solve them,

10200
07:44:18.050 --> 07:44:20.050
you can actually like turn them into a bot

10201
07:44:20.050 --> 07:44:21.930
and just like keep them running forever.

10202
07:44:21.930 --> 07:44:23.490
And eventually like that's,

10203
07:44:23.490 --> 07:44:25.610
those bots are gonna grow by a lot.

10204
07:44:26.730 --> 07:44:27.570
But yeah, it's still,

10205
07:44:27.570 --> 07:44:29.170
it's an interesting like paradigm

10206
07:44:29.170 --> 07:44:31.810
to create a company with rock bots.

10207
07:44:31.810 --> 07:44:33.320
Yeah, yeah.

10208
07:44:33.320 --> 07:44:34.560
Yeah, Adam, go ahead.

10209
07:44:34.560 --> 07:44:35.920
Sorry, can we, a production team,

10210
07:44:35.920 --> 07:44:37.440
can we take my screen off?

10211
07:44:40.280 --> 07:44:44.440
Yeah, I think the thing I'm also reflecting on

10212
07:44:44.440 --> 07:44:45.680
is like, you know, the,

10213
07:44:45.680 --> 07:44:49.360
for me, the process of building a game and a game studio.

10214
07:44:49.360 --> 07:44:51.280
A lot of the, you know,

10215
07:44:51.280 --> 07:44:52.520
even though our first product,

10216
07:44:52.560 --> 07:44:55.000
our first game isn't really that good.

10217
07:44:55.000 --> 07:44:57.880
I still keep coming back to this idea that

10218
07:44:57.880 --> 07:45:01.760
optimizing and thinking about your workflow, right?

10219
07:45:01.760 --> 07:45:04.320
Like how you actually get work done

10220
07:45:04.320 --> 07:45:08.320
is so powerful when you have growth bot by your side

10221
07:45:08.320 --> 07:45:10.920
and automating and doing things.

10222
07:45:10.920 --> 07:45:12.880
Because, you know, we can again,

10223
07:45:12.880 --> 07:45:15.080
take the learnings you reiterate fast

10224
07:45:15.080 --> 07:45:17.600
and ship the next, ship a next game

10225
07:45:17.600 --> 07:45:19.200
or ship the next application.

10226
07:45:21.240 --> 07:45:22.440
I think a lot about building products

10227
07:45:22.440 --> 07:45:25.360
is not just the initial splashy launch,

10228
07:45:25.360 --> 07:45:28.080
but also how you keep improving it as you...

10229
07:45:28.080 --> 07:45:29.080
Getting the flywheels in.

10230
07:45:29.080 --> 07:45:30.080
Getting the flywheel.

10231
07:45:30.080 --> 07:45:30.920
Right.

10232
07:45:30.920 --> 07:45:33.440
And also exercising some restraint, right?

10233
07:45:33.440 --> 07:45:37.720
Like with AI, you can literally build anything you want.

10234
07:45:37.720 --> 07:45:41.320
So you can have products that just have a million features

10235
07:45:41.320 --> 07:45:43.520
and they're not any good, right?

10236
07:45:43.520 --> 07:45:45.360
And so there's this,

10237
07:45:45.360 --> 07:45:47.560
there's almost like this discipline

10238
07:45:47.560 --> 07:45:49.080
that we now have to have, right?

10239
07:45:49.080 --> 07:45:52.480
When there's an abundance of intelligence

10240
07:45:52.480 --> 07:45:56.040
and ability to build to do that.

10241
07:45:56.040 --> 07:45:56.880
So...

10242
07:45:56.880 --> 07:45:57.720
Yeah.

10243
07:45:57.720 --> 07:45:58.680
One of the things we talk a lot about internally is

10244
07:45:58.680 --> 07:46:00.120
what are we going to unshift

10245
07:46:00.120 --> 07:46:02.160
and just having this meant constant mentality

10246
07:46:02.160 --> 07:46:04.040
that there's stuff you should remove from the product

10247
07:46:04.040 --> 07:46:06.160
to simplify it, make it easier.

10248
07:46:06.160 --> 07:46:08.560
And I think we did a decent job of that, right?

10249
07:46:08.560 --> 07:46:09.520
We didn't feature bloat.

10250
07:46:09.520 --> 07:46:11.200
We came in with a lot of feature ideas.

10251
07:46:11.200 --> 07:46:12.480
I'm thinking back to yesterday

10252
07:46:12.480 --> 07:46:14.120
when we had our initial whiteboard,

10253
07:46:14.120 --> 07:46:16.600
we had these really complicated stat blocks

10254
07:46:16.600 --> 07:46:17.640
for each character.

10255
07:46:17.640 --> 07:46:21.400
We had a whole plan to add different battlefields.

10256
07:46:21.400 --> 07:46:22.520
And I think what really,

10257
07:46:22.520 --> 07:46:23.760
at least let us get this out today

10258
07:46:23.760 --> 07:46:25.760
was making sure we pared that down a little bit

10259
07:46:25.760 --> 07:46:27.320
and really just focused on the core loop.

10260
07:46:27.320 --> 07:46:29.400
And that went through its own iterations,

10261
07:46:29.400 --> 07:46:31.280
but I think that actually made a really big difference

10262
07:46:31.280 --> 07:46:32.600
to getting something launched.

10263
07:46:32.600 --> 07:46:34.600
And then, you know, also something that we think

10264
07:46:34.600 --> 07:46:35.800
ended up looking pretty good in the end.

10265
07:46:35.800 --> 07:46:37.160
So, yeah.

10266
07:46:37.160 --> 07:46:38.000
One final question.

10267
07:46:38.000 --> 07:46:40.760
Like if you, if someone were to ask you like,

10268
07:46:40.760 --> 07:46:42.560
I want to build a company with Crockbot,

10269
07:46:42.560 --> 07:46:45.680
what are like the top three things you would tell them?

10270
07:46:45.680 --> 07:46:48.170
Ooh.

10271
07:46:48.170 --> 07:46:50.490
It helps to like know exactly what you're doing before.

10272
07:46:50.490 --> 07:46:51.810
Like, okay, so here's a good example.

10273
07:46:51.810 --> 07:46:53.530
We talked to a guest yesterday.

10274
07:46:53.530 --> 07:46:55.010
I can't remember exactly which guest.

10275
07:46:55.010 --> 07:46:56.690
So maybe one of you can help me.

10276
07:46:56.690 --> 07:46:57.530
And they were like,

10277
07:46:57.530 --> 07:46:58.530
oh, you guys want to do an event pop-up?

10278
07:46:58.530 --> 07:47:00.170
And then they just rattled off like 10 things

10279
07:47:00.170 --> 07:47:01.970
that I'd never thought about doing an event pop-up before.

10280
07:47:01.970 --> 07:47:03.730
Like permitting, catering,

10281
07:47:03.730 --> 07:47:05.810
what it means to serve hot food versus cold food

10282
07:47:05.810 --> 07:47:06.810
if you need a kitchen.

10283
07:47:06.810 --> 07:47:09.130
And I was just like, oh, like that's all stuff

10284
07:47:09.130 --> 07:47:09.970
I've never thought about

10285
07:47:09.970 --> 07:47:11.090
because I've never actually done it.

10286
07:47:11.090 --> 07:47:12.290
And so a large part of like,

10287
07:47:12.290 --> 07:47:15.170
as it turns out, like doing something is actually

10288
07:47:15.170 --> 07:47:17.250
maybe unintuitively actually just doing it

10289
07:47:17.290 --> 07:47:18.130
and then figuring out like,

10290
07:47:18.130 --> 07:47:19.410
oh, I'm not good at this thing

10291
07:47:19.410 --> 07:47:20.730
and I need to learn these things.

10292
07:47:20.730 --> 07:47:21.970
That's like what makes a professional

10293
07:47:21.970 --> 07:47:23.330
and someone that like does a business well

10294
07:47:23.330 --> 07:47:24.890
is like, you know exactly what you're doing.

10295
07:47:24.890 --> 07:47:26.530
So if you're going to build a business with Crockbot,

10296
07:47:26.530 --> 07:47:28.210
like build a business around something

10297
07:47:28.210 --> 07:47:29.610
you already know how to do well.

10298
07:47:29.610 --> 07:47:30.890
And then that makes it a lot easier

10299
07:47:30.890 --> 07:47:32.330
versus someone that comes in and says,

10300
07:47:32.330 --> 07:47:34.490
oh, I'm just going to like make a bunch of money.

10301
07:47:34.490 --> 07:47:36.270
And as it turns out,

10302
07:47:36.270 --> 07:47:38.050
