10313
07:47:55.690 --> 07:47:57.910
Like we're really lucky to have a bunch of guests

10314
07:47:57.910 --> 07:48:00.490
as Matt called out that kind of helped steer us

10315
07:48:00.490 --> 07:48:01.770
throughout these three days.

10316
07:48:01.770 --> 07:48:04.490
But a lot of the bots we created to go learn things

10317
07:48:04.490 --> 07:48:06.070
like we have game designer bots

10318
07:48:06.070 --> 07:48:08.050
who learned how to do game design

10319
07:48:08.050 --> 07:48:09.850
by just learning from the best games.

10320
07:48:09.850 --> 07:48:13.250
And one of the things that maybe I undervalued

10321
07:48:13.250 --> 07:48:15.610
before this was you can give the bots lots of context,

10322
07:48:15.730 --> 07:48:18.570
you can sort of teach them all the things they need to know.

10323
07:48:18.570 --> 07:48:21.050
We had someone earlier on the stream talking about how

10324
07:48:21.050 --> 07:48:23.610
whenever they're entering into a new discipline,

10325
07:48:23.610 --> 07:48:25.510
they tell the bot to go take a bunch of courses

10326
07:48:25.510 --> 07:48:26.350
on the internet.

10327
07:48:26.350 --> 07:48:27.970
And I never really thought, I never thought of that idea.

10328
07:48:27.970 --> 07:48:29.770
But you sort of think of these bots

10329
07:48:29.770 --> 07:48:32.010
because they sort of learn and evolve over time,

10330
07:48:32.010 --> 07:48:34.570
you can kind of encourage them to learn

10331
07:48:34.570 --> 07:48:35.850
the things you want them to learn.

10332
07:48:35.850 --> 07:48:38.050
And so maybe another angle to what Matt said

10333
07:48:38.050 --> 07:48:40.810
